  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of dip at a place is $37^{\\circ}$ and the vertical component of the earth's magnetic field is $6 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$. The earth's magnetic field at this place is $\\left(\\tan 37^{\\circ}=\\frac{3}{4}\\right)$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$7 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$6 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$10^{-4} \\mathrm{~T}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\tan \\theta=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{H}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\left[\\because \\tan 37^{\\circ}=\\frac{3}{4}\\right]$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{V}=\\frac{3}{4} \\mathrm{H}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{V}=6 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{H}=\\frac{4}{3} \\times 6 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}=8 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~T}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{B}_{\\text {total }}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{V}^{2}+\\mathrm{H}^{2}}=\\sqrt{(36+64)} \\times 10^{-5}$\r\n\r\n$=10 \\times 10^{-5}=10^{-4} \\mathrm{~T} .$"
  }
}